  "narrative": "The new results materially support the robustness of the accepted TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss associations and reveal one additional large dataset-level association. H14/H15 show that the positive TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss contrasts remain large and precise in the dominant Avana-library subset. H16/H17 show that each association persists when the other accepted loss is excluded, reducing the concern that TP53 and KEAP1 effects are merely mutual confounding by co-occurrence. H27/H28 show the same positive associations in the smaller Ky-library subset, although with wider intervals as expected from smaller cell sizes. H20/H21 do not support a scientifically meaningful positive effect modification by high versus low screen ROC-AUC for TP53 or KEAP1; the interaction estimates are small and intervals include zero, so I reject those heterogeneity claims in the registered direction and close them. H18 is a registered positive TP53-by-KEAP1 interaction; the estimate is small, interval includes zero, and the point estimate is well below the 0.15-unit threshold, so there is no evidence for a scientifically meaningful positive interaction and I reject/close it. H25 MTAP loss is near null and rejected. H22 CDKN2A loss in TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact cells is directionally supportive for stronger dependency but its signed point estimate is 0.144, below the 0.15 threshold despite a positive lower bound; I keep it unresolved/active rather than accept. H26 SMARCA4 loss is a new large positive signed effect in the registered negative direction, i.e. raw SMARCA4 loss is associated with a substantially more negative dependency_composite, meaning stronger composite dependency, by about 0.80 units with a tight interval entirely above the threshold in the claimed signed direction. Because this is a new accepted large dataset association and independent replication is informative before over-interpreting it, I accept H26 as a dataset-level association and request independent validation. The new proposals test SMARCA4-loss robustness and independence from TP53/KEAP1 co-occurrence, plus a related SWI/SNF-component loss hypothesis for ARID1A. These remain associations in this dataset, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current accepted dataset associations: H3 KEAP1 loss positive/validated; H13 TP53 loss positive; H14/H15 Avana robustness accepted; H16/H17 co-loss-excluded robustness accepted; H27/H28 Ky-library robustness accepted; H26 SMARCA4 loss negative/stronger dependency accepted pending validation. Interpretation: signed positive for H26 means raw exposed-minus-comparator is negative because direction is -1, i.e. SMARCA4 loss lowers dependency_composite and therefore indicates stronger dependency. Null/rejected: H18 TP53 x KEAP1 interaction positive, H20/H21 screen_roc_auc interaction positive for TP53/KEAP1, H25 MTAP loss negative. H22 CDKN2A in TP53/KEAP1-intact cells remains unresolved: signed estimate +0.144 [0.075,0.213], below 0.15 point threshold but upper above threshold. H4 overall CDKN2A remains unresolved similarly. Validation requested for H26 because it is newly accepted and large. Next analysis priorities: conditional SMARCA4 loss in TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, SMARCA4 in Avana and Ky libraries, ARID1A loss negative as a related broad predictor. If conditional SMARCA4 remains large, it supports an independent dataset-level association; if attenuated, narrow or reassess. All findings remain dataset associations, not causality or generalizability.",
