 "narrative":"The independent validation result for H26 confirms the discovery SMARCA4-loss association. H26 was registered in the negative direction, so the signed positive validation estimate +0.800 (stringent validation interval [0.705, 0.895]) corresponds to a raw SMARCA4-loss mean difference about -0.80 composite dependency-score units relative to SMARCA4-intact samples. Because more negative dependency_composite values mean stronger dependency, the scientifically meaningful interpretation is that SMARCA4 loss is strongly associated with stronger composite dependency within this dataset. The validation estimate is almost identical to discovery (+0.804 [0.742, 0.867]) and its lower bound remains far above the 0.15-unit threshold even under a stringent independent interval. I therefore keep H26 accepted and active. With H3 (KEAP1 loss associated with weaker dependency, validated), H13 (TP53 loss associated with weaker dependency), and H26 (SMARCA4 loss associated with stronger dependency), the current evidence supports three large dataset-level predictor associations rather than weak associations. However, the SMARCA4 claim remains a dataset-level association, not causality, not a gene-specific knockout dependency inference, and not external generalizability. The most informative next analyses are the registered conditional/robustness checks: H33 tests SMARCA4 loss among TP53-intact and KEAP1-intact samples, H34/H35 test library-specific stability, and H36 tests related ARID1A loss as a specificity/biological-plausibility probe. If H33 remains large, SMARCA4 loss is associated with composite dependency independent of the other two dominant accepted predictors; if it attenuates strongly, the original claim should be narrowed or reassessed as dependent on co-occurring TP53/KEAP1 status. H4/H22 CDKN2A remain unresolved near threshold and should only be accepted if future evidence consistently exceeds 0.15.",
 "research_notes":"Current accepted dataset-level associations: H3 KEAP1 loss positive (validated; weaker dependency); H13 TP53 loss positive (weaker dependency); H14/H15/H16/H17/H27/H28 show TP53/KEAP1 robustness across Avana, Ky, and excluded co-loss subsets; H26 SMARCA4 loss negative/stronger dependency (validated). H26 validation: signed +0.800 [0.705,0.895], consistent with discovery +0.804 [0.742,0.867]. Rejected/null: STK11, KRAS, MYC amp, markers D/E/F, KRAS x STK11, MTAP loss, TP53 x KEAP1 interaction, screen ROC AUC interactions. Unresolved: CDKN2A overall and in TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, both point estimates about 0.14, below 0.15 but intervals include above-threshold. Next run H33-H36: SMARCA4 in TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, SMARCA4 Avana/Ky robustness, ARID1A loss negative. If SMARCA4 conditional effect attenuates, narrow H26. If ARID1A is null/opposite, avoid overgeneralizing to all SWI/SNF losses. All conclusions remain dataset associations only."
